## Objective

Create only `../runbooks/R0001.md` from manifest batch B0001. Its precise
contract is IMP-0001, "Bootstrap reproducible shared project baseline". It is
not permission to implement the game or resolve GATE-0001.

## Context packet

Read `../PROJECT_BRIEF.md`, `../specification/01-product-brief.md#release-definition`,
`../specification/03-technical-contract.md#architecture-and-requirement-traceability`,
`../planning/implementation-catalogue-index.json` (IMP-0001), and the B0001/R0001
manifest records. Use `../../../runbooks/TEMPLATE.md` for the Supervisor shape.

## Output list

- `../runbooks/R0001.md` only; metadata must use `task_id: R0001`, `sequence: 1`, `source_catalogue_ids: IMP-0001`, `authoring_batch: B0001`, `factory_stages: F011,F012,F013`, and the manifest provenance/asset values.

## Required authoring content

Give R0001 a small, precise objective; dependencies; relevant requirement IDs;
owned files, data, and interfaces; required behaviour; non-goals; web/PWA
platform differences; verification commands and evidence; observable acceptance
criteria; and an `## Asset assessment` explaining that no asset is needed and
incidental asset creation is prohibited. Include all required standard front
matter, including `asset_impact: not_applicable`, blank `asset_ids`, and the
non-empty provenance fields exactly as the manifest records them.

## Validation procedure

Before writing, stop if R0001 exists with a different ID, catalogue mapping,
provenance, dependency set, or output owner. After writing, load it with
`supervisor.runbooks.load_task`, compare every metadata value and dependency
against the manifest, and confirm it has all required sections.

## Checkpoint and update procedure

Update only B0001's manifest state/checkpoint after successful validation.
Retain R0001 and its ID on any failure; repair that one path on resume.

## Stop condition

Stop after R0001. Do not create another R file, choose a framework, or pass GATE-0001.

## Acceptance criteria

- Exactly one R-series runbook, R0001, is created for the allocated IMP-0001 contract.
- R0001 is a bounded implementation task with the required sections, metadata, provenance, and explicit no-asset assessment.
- Existing conflicting R0001 content causes a stop and report rather than an overwrite.
- Manifest ownership and checkpoint state are updated only after structural validation passes.

